<spell-notebook "text theming">
	<header level="1">
		Text
		<header>A text is used to style some inline text with a simple color.</>
	</>
	<text-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-text-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or on the
			inner box through `::part(text)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a private
			alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- The hues themselves are global colour tokens (`--ui-red` and friends): change those to recolour every component
			  at once.
			- The component's tokens share the `--ui-text-` prefix with the GLOBAL text colours (`--ui-text-color`,
			  `--ui-text-muted` ...); the table below lists only the component's own.
			- Never set the `--_ui-text-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every text on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-text-disabled-opacity: 0.6;
			}
			/* one region */
			.headline {
			  --ui-text-line-height: 1.2;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-text" playground>
				<p>This is <ui-text color="red">red inline text</> and <ui-text color="blue">this is blue inline text</> and <ui-text color="purple">this is purple inline text</>.</>
				<p>
					<ui-text color="primary">Primary</>
					<ui-text color="secondary">Secondary</>
					<ui-text color="orange">Orange</>
					<ui-text color="yellow">Yellow</>
					<ui-text color="olive">Olive</>
					<ui-text color="green">Green</>
					<ui-text color="teal">Teal</>
					<ui-text color="violet">Violet</>
					<ui-text color="pink">Pink</>
					<ui-text color="brown">Brown</>
					<ui-text color="grey">Grey</>
					<ui-text color="black">Black</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu in the header (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes text's colours and fonts through
			the shared tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
